---
description: Resolve the requested local delivery or continuity outcome from current owned evidence, and choose an authorized continuation.
budget: { maxTurns: 40 }
args:
  goal: string
returns: LocalDeliveryReport
---
Work toward the caller's actual delivery outcome. Discover the owned conversations and use the investigation branch to establish the relevant current audience, retained note and acknowledgement. Choose the scope and further investigation from the goal and actual findings; available rooms are not a mandatory checklist. Receipts for another message, room, recipient or revision remain evidence about that different delivery.

The decision branch can reconcile the evidence. For a read-only answer, return an accurately bound report with its important limits; do not send merely to resolve uncertainty. For a requested conditional follow-up, establish its condition and exact current recipient first. Use the settlement boundary for any new send: it checks the selected observed room and native send permission, composes the requested note in its own semantic branch, and retains the real attempt/readback. An interrupted submit is not permission to submit the same note again. Report actual delivered, unconfirmed or held state, rather than turning a plan into proof of delivery. Preserve contradictions and uncertainty needed to answer the request.
